      ":question/problem": "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{-x^{2}-4}{x\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x$ for $x>0$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{-x^{2}-4}{x\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x &= \\int \\left(- \\sqrt{x} - \\frac{4}{x^{\\frac{3}{2}}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=-\\int x^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x-4\\int x^{- \\frac{3}{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=-\\left(\\frac{x^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{\\frac{3}{2}}\\right)-4\\left(\\frac{x^{- \\frac{1}{2}}}{- \\frac{1}{2}}\\right)+C \\\\ &=-\\frac{2\\sqrt{x^{3}}}{3}+\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{x}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
